# Soul Rules (P0) — Immutable Invariants

These rules can NEVER be violated regardless of context, task type, or agent layer.

## S-1 — Dispatcher-Not-Implementer Invariant

Dispatcher agents (Project, Wave) MUST NOT perform work directly. Only Task Agents execute actual work — writing code, running tests, authoring documents, performing reviews. L0-L1 agents MAY use Read, Glob, Grep, SemanticSearch for planning/orchestration. L0-L1 MUST NOT use Write, StrReplace, Shell (for code/test/build), or EditNotebook to implement. Trivial exception: single file, < 20 lines.

## S-2 — No Absolute Paths in Agent Files

All paths in dispatch messages, status reports, artifact references, SKILL.md, CLAUDE.md, and all reference documents must be relative to the repository root. Absolute filesystem paths are prohibited. External resources must be referenced via their remote URL.

Sources: CO-4, SF-5.

## S-3 — Test Coverage Floor

Coverage has two distinct requirements:

- **Global target:** repository-wide test coverage MUST be at least 90%.
- **Per-module floor:** every new or modified Python module MUST maintain at
  least 75% test coverage. New modules must have > 0% coverage before merge.

Verify the global target with:
```
python -m pytest tests/ --cov=devolaflow --cov-report=term-missing
```

Source: CP-2.

## S-4 — No Ghost Features

Every feature listed in CHANGELOG.md must have corresponding working code, tests, and (if applicable) documentation. Do not add CHANGELOG entries for code that does not yet exist.

Source: CP-1.

## S-5 — No Silent Failures

Never suppress errors with try-catch (or equivalents) without logging, re-throwing, or returning explicit error states. Only ignore errors if explicitly requested for non-critical "best-effort" execution.

## S-6 — Protected Branch Workflow

NEVER push directly to protected branches (main, master, yc_dev, production). Always create a new feature branch, commit changes there, and propose a Merge Request or Pull Request.

## S-7 — External Resource URLs

External tools and benchmarks MUST be referenced by their remote GitHub URL. Local clone paths MUST NOT be hardcoded in any agent-facing file.

Sources: SF-6, SI-7.

## S-8 — No Writes Outside Active Change Owned Files

When an L2 Task Agent is operating inside a `change-driven` workflow with an
active change folder (`.local/.agent/active/<change-id>/`), it MUST NOT modify
any file outside the union of:
1. paths listed in `.local/.agent/active/<change-id>/owned_files.txt`
2. the change folder itself
3. `.local/.agent/handoff/` (only its own outbox; append-only — see S-9)

Violations:
- Detected at file-write time via `lifecycle/check_file_ownership` hook
- In `mode: lite` — warn + log
- In `mode: full` (or STRICT) — block + escalate per P4

Exceptions:
- Trivial single-file edits < 20 lines (P1 trivial waiver also applies here)
- L0/L1 dispatcher reads (Read/Glob/Grep/SemanticSearch) are unrestricted

Source: v15-ADR-008 §S-8.

## S-9 — Handoff Envelopes Are Append-Only

Once a `<from>__<to>__<change-id>__<seq>.yaml` envelope exists in
`.local/.agent/handoff/`, it MUST NOT be modified or deleted by any agent.

To convey new information, the agent MUST author a new envelope with `seq+1`.

Rationale: append-only ledger prevents silent overwrites between agents
operating in parallel. Mirrors P5 (Artifacts as Contracts).

Enforcement: `tests/test_handoff_envelope_immutable.py` lints CI runs;
`lifecycle/check_envelope_append_only` hook blocks at write time in STRICT mode.

Source: v15-ADR-008 §S-9.

## S-10 — Prompt-Side Governance Contract Embedding

Every dispatch payload returned by
`src/devolaflow/feedback.py::ProposalGenerator.generate_round_dispatch`
MUST be visible to the lifecycle hook chain
(`pre_dispatch` → `post_dispatch`) via
`devolaflow.lifecycle.run_hooks(event, payload, strict=False)`. The
hook chain is the canonical prompt-side enforcement surface for
governance contracts:

- `pre_dispatch` validates dispatch CONTENT (acceptance criteria,
  owned files, schema compliance).
- `post_dispatch` is the future-extensibility slot for governance
  contracts (Soul-set version embedding, rule-manifest URL,
  reinforcement state); the default is a permissive no-op that
  preserves cache bytes.

R5 strict triple codification:
1. **Hook**: `lifecycle/__init__.py::DEFAULT_EVENTS` includes both
   `pre_dispatch` and `post_dispatch`; both wired to permissive
   defaults that NEVER mutate the payload.
2. **Schema**: `feedback.py::generate_round_dispatch` calls the hook
   chain on every return path (round-1 pass-through, no-reinforcement,
   reinforcement-applied).
3. **Test**: `tests/test_dispatch_emission_runs_hooks.py` asserts the
   hook is invoked exactly once per dispatch in permissive mode AND
   that the returned dispatch is byte-identical to the control when no
   extras register.

Enforcement: a dispatch path that bypasses the hook chain is a release
blocker. Detected at test time via the regression suite above; the
permissive try/except in `feedback._emit_dispatch` ensures a buggy
custom handler raises a WARNING log (per S-5) without aborting the
dispatch.

Exceptions:
- None. The hook chain MUST run on every dispatch — even when there
  are no extras to invoke (the default no-op handlers run in O(1)).

Source: v15-ADR-008 §S-10.

# Architecture Rules (P1) — Core Architectural Decisions

## A-1 — 3-Layer Agent Hierarchy (P1–P5)

The dispatcher boundary is defined by S-1. S-1 applies to Project→Wave→Task:
L0/L1 dispatch only; L2 executes within ~8K; L0/L1 receive ~5K. Inter-layer
messages MUST use typed YAML (TaskDispatch, StatusReport, ExceptionEscalation);
free-form messages are prohibited. Every loop has `max_iterations`; failures
classify as retry/escalate/abort and escalate Task→Wave→Project→Human.
Artifacts are typed, producer-written contracts; no shared/bidirectional state.

## A-2 — P6 Preserve Cached Prefix (Cache-Layout Governance v2)

Dispatch payloads MUST honor `schemas/lean-dispatch.yaml#layout_invariant`;
call `devolaflow.compressor.assert_dispatch_layout(payload)` before sending.
New top-level keys MUST append after position 17 in the live schema; reordering is a release
blocker.

### A-2.1 — Frozen Prefix (positions 1-12)

The first 12 `canonical_order` positions are the **FROZEN PREFIX** and their
byte-stable rendering is the LLM cache prefix. Reordering, renaming, or
removing one is a release blocker; enforce with
`devolaflow.compressor.assert_layout_spec_invariant`.

### A-2.2 — Append-Only Tail (positions 13+)

Positions 13+ are **APPEND-ONLY**: new top-level keys land at N+1, never lower.

### A-2.3 — Nest-vs-Append Decision Rule

Per v9-ADR-002 D3, **NEST** when behavior modifies/reuses an existing block or
is co-present; **APPEND** only for orthogonal/cross-block state. Independently
optional fields may use either, but prefer NEST; every append can extend the
serialized cache prefix.

### A-2.4 — Multi-Baseline Byte Test (Tiered Retention)

CI runs `tests/test_layout_invariant_multi_baseline.py` against
`layout_invariant_v*.yaml`; witness drift fails. Schema bumps add a new golden
and retain every existing witness.

* **Tier A** immutable layout witnesses in
  `benchmarks/devolaflow_context/baselines/`.
* **Tier B** current + previous two
  `.local/telemetry/baselines/harness_baseline_<cycle>.json`.
* **Tier C** older baselines in
  `docs/cycle-archive/<cycle>/harness/`; history is retained.

## A-3 — Context Token Budgets

`workflow-system/agent/context_profiles.yaml` MUST define explicit per-task
budgets, allocated by priority: critical, then important, then supplementary.
Layer budgets: L0 Project ~5K (template/status), L1 Wave ~5K
(tasks/dependencies/evidence), L2 Task ~8K (spec/owned files/rules).

## A-4 — Source-of-Truth Spec Location (M-004 ADR)

`.local/memory/specs/<domain>/spec.md` is behavioral SSOT; per-change
`.local/.agent/active/<id>/spec.md` contains ADDED/MODIFIED/REMOVED deltas.
SSOT mutates ONLY at archive time after a passed gate (W-3/SI-3 ≥8.5 minor,
≥9.0 major); its `mergeability_check` (v8.2.5 reporter) must pass before merge.

## A-5 — Single-Source-of-Truth Registry Pattern

Every domain registry surface MUST have **exactly one owner module**. Consumers
import its registration data and MUST NOT redefine or shadow it. Parity and
derived-view status are enforced by `tests/ghost/test_registries.py`.

| # | Registry surface | Owner module / file |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Plugin registry | `workflow-system/agent/knowledge/runtime-plugins.yaml`, loaded by `devolaflow.plugins.installer.load_registry`; `plugins.yaml` is a derived view, pinned by `tests/test_plugins.py::TestV15PluginRegistryUnification` |
| 2 | Memory-router case type | `src/devolaflow/memory_router/cache.py::MemoryCase` |
| 3 | Host Support Contract | `workflow-system/agent/hosts.yaml`, loaded by `devolaflow.host_contract.load_host_contract`; `manifest.yaml::install_profiles` is derived |
| 4 | Local archive adapters (registered surfaces and archive destinations) | `src/devolaflow/local/archive_adapters.py::ARCHIVE_ADAPTERS` |

### A-5.1 — Single-Owner Invariant

Adding a surface requires one owner and routing all consumers through it.
Splitting registration data invalidates cache reasoning and is a release
blocker. `tests/ghost/test_registries.py::test_registry_single_owner` uses an
AST walk to reject multiple module-level definitions.

### A-5.2 — DEFAULT_ALLOWLIST Hygiene

`DEFAULT_ALLOWLIST` covers public APIs without in-repo callers; SSOT registry
symbols MUST NOT appear there. Enforce with `_check_allowlist_domain_overlap`
and `tests/test_dead_apis.py`.

## A-6 — Workspace Engagement Auto-Activation

When `DEVOLAFLOW_AGENT_WORKSPACE=1` AND complexity ≥ STANDARD per the
SKILL.md §"Quick Action Decision" table, L0 MUST scaffold
`.local/.agent/active/<id>/` with `entrance.md` before dispatching the first
L1 stage.
Default-OFF; rule is normative for opted-in operators.

### A-6.1 — Classification surface
Complexity classification is the output of
`devolaflow.skills.change_activation.classify_complexity(...)`; the
activation verdict is `activation_verdict(complexity, env_flag,
opt_out)`. The three-valued verdict (MUST_OPEN_CHANGE /
SHOULD_OPEN_CHANGE / NO_CHANGE) is the sole public contract —
operators rely on the string values.

### A-6.2 — Opt-in gate
`DEVOLAFLOW_AGENT_WORKSPACE=1` is REUSED per W-20 (same activation
surface as v9.1.1 PV-01 SKILL.md §"Workspace Engagement (Read at
Session Start)" and as the v9.1.3 PV-03 `pre_handoff` hook will use).
NO new env flag. Absent or any value other than the literal string
"1" = default-OFF (R5 strict).

### A-6.3 — Opt-out escape hatch
Users may pass `--no-change` to `/devola:propose` to suppress
scaffolding even when the env flag is ON. No other opt-out channel
exists (keeps the surface auditable).

### A-6.4 — Enforcement
Prompt-side: SKILL.md §"Quick Action Decision" sub-table cites this
rule. CI-side: `tests/test_change_activation_heuristic.py` pins the
three verdict cases + opt-out behaviour + byte-stable no-op when env
flag absent.

### A-6.5 — Task/Change Folder Entrance Materialization
When an agent creates or opens a task/change folder under
`.local/.agent/active/<id>/` or `.local/tasks/<name>/`, `entrance.md` MUST be
written in the first artifact batch, unless the programmatic scaffold
(`scaffold_change_folder` / `Change.to_active_folder`) performs that write.

## A-7 — Cascade-Depth Invariant for Standard+ Dispatches

When `gate.cascade_required` is `true` (STANDARD/COMPLEX from
`devolaflow.skills.change_activation::cascade_requirement`), dispatch MUST
traverse at least `gate.cascade_min_layers` layers before L2 (default 3:
L0 Project→L1 Wave→L2 Task). SIMPLE/TRIVIAL returns
`"CASCADE_OPTIONAL"` and bypasses this rule.

### A-7.1 — Conditional strict enforcement

For `"CASCADE_REQUIRED"`, STRICT
`validate_cascade_gate_fields` returns `None` on pass and raises
`CascadeViolationError` on the first invalid field/depth violation; declared
`cascade_min_layers` is validated at face value. For `"CASCADE_OPTIONAL"`,
validation is skipped and legacy dispatches without fields remain byte-identical.

### A-7.2 — Trivial waiver

Per A-1 P1, L0 may directly author a single-file edit under 20 lines. At
payload level, omitted `gate.cascade_required` (v11.0.x default) skips
validation; `populate_cascade_gate_fields` returns an unchanged deep copy for
SIMPLE/TRIVIAL.

### A-7.3 — Operator override

`force_no_change=True` bypasses workspace activation and is orthogonal to A-7.

### A-7.4 — Enforcement surface

* Tests: `tests/test_cascade_enforcement.py` covers strict, compatibility,
  skip, propagation, and immutability.
* Runtime: `validate_cascade_gate_fields` returns `None` or raises
  `CascadeViolationError`; `populate_cascade_gate_fields` defaults to 3.
* Audit: `scripts/audit_layer_usage.py --threshold N` is strict by default
  (exit 1 below `cascade_ratio` N); `--no-strict` opts out; default N=0.30.
* Schema: `gate.cascade_required: bool` and `gate.cascade_min_layers: int`
  nest under `gate`; absence is canonical.

# Conventions Rules (P2) — Coding & Format Standards

## C-1 — Pre-Commit Verification Checklist

Before committing, verify `python -m pytest tests/ -q`, `ruff check src/ tests/`,
`ruff format --check src/ tests/`, no absolute paths in agent-facing files,
and CHANGELOG updates for user-visible changes.

Source: CP-7.

## C-2 — Lean Message Format

TaskDispatch and StatusReport MUST use the lean formats in
`schemas/lean-dispatch.yaml` and `schemas/lean-report.yaml`; verbose prose is
prohibited. Use verbatim `key_facts` and cause→effect notation. Predecessor
`key_facts` and report `delta` MUST be source extractions: never paraphrase
paths, errors, metrics, or commit hashes (CO-1/CO-2).

Source: CO-1; CO-2.

## C-4 — Tiered Line Budget

Tiered ceilings: Default `<500` lines for `workflow-system/agent/SKILL.md`;
Large `≤1000` for `references/*.md` (26 files); XL `≤1600` for
`examples/*.md` (3 files).

Verify with:
```bash
wc -l workflow-system/agent/SKILL.md workflow-system/agent/references/*.md workflow-system/agent/examples/*.md
python -m pytest tests/test_integration.py::test_skill_md_under_500_lines tests/test_reference_size_budgets.py -v
```

### Required SKILL.md Frontmatter Keys

Frontmatter MUST include ALL: `id`, `version`, `purpose`, `triggers`, `tier`,
`token_estimate`, `last_updated`, `name`, `description`. `description` MUST
state WHEN/WHY to activate, not WHAT it does. Verify with the C-4 commands.
Source: SF-1; SF-2.

## C-6 — Version Consistency

The version MUST match `src/devolaflow/__init__.py::__version__` in all 7:

1. SKILL.md frontmatter, banner, and `Current version:`
2. `workflow-skill.yaml` identity
3. `pyproject.toml`
4. `scripts/generate_human_docs.py::SOURCE_VERSION`
5. `tests/test_smoke.py`
6. README example (`DevolaFlow vX.Y.Z`)
7. `packages/npm/package.json` (publish workflow tag check)

The README badge is **DERIVED, not pattern-managed (v14.4.0 G-031)**: it is a
dynamic TOML derivation; benchmark-results derives the displayed version from
`version-timeline/versions.json`. Its marked `file://` `SAMPLE_DATA` fallback
MAY lag and is not synced. Use
`scripts/bump_version.py`, then run `python -m pytest tests/test_version.py -v`.

Source: SF-3. Absorbs W-10 (CP-3) — v15.0.0 fold per v15-ADR-004; see v15-ADR-008 §1.

## C-7 — Valid Reference Links

Every `references/xxx.md` cited by SKILL.md MUST exist under
`workflow-system/agent/references/`. The SF-4 set is owned by
`tests/ghost/test_registries.py::_SF4_REFERENCE_SET` and pinned by
`test_skill_reference_links_match_sf4_set`. A new reference MUST add (a) the
file, (b) the SF-4 entry, (c) a SKILL Tier-2 row, and (d) the
`workflow-system/agent/manifest.yaml::references` entry. That manifest is the
install SSOT for `sync_cursor_skill.py::MIRRORED_FILES`, `scripts/install.sh`,
and `devola-init`; parity is tested by `tests/test_install_manifest.py`.
`scripts/scaffold_reference.py` automates (a), (c), and (d). Source: SF-4.

### Lightweight Agent Workspace Artifacts

Files in `.local/.agent/active/<change-id>/` and
`.local/.agent/archive/<date>-<id>/` use these token budgets:

| File | Soft | Hard |
|---|---:|---:|
| goal.md | 200 | 400 |
| checklist.md | 1200 | 2400 |
| stage.md | 400 | 800 |
| preflight.md | 600 | 1200 |
| harness_preflight.md | 800 | 1600 |
| pathfinder_report.md | 800 | 1600 |
| spec.md | 1500 | 3000 |
| STATUS.yaml | 150 | 300 |
| owned_files.txt | 50 | 100 |
| Handoff envelope | 600 | 1200 |
| evidence/ | No token limit | ≤ 10 KB/file; ≤ 50 KB/directory |
| entrance.md | 400/800 |

Soft budget overages warn; Hard ceiling breaches fail commit.

`.local/human/` uses token-only budgets (line/word counts are guidance):

| `input/constitution.md` | 800/1500 |
| `input/requirements.md`, `input/requirements/<domain>.md` | 1200/2500 |
| `input/amendments/<date>-<slug>.md` | 400/800 |
| `output/DIGEST.md` | 600/1000 |
| `output/convergence/<version>-convergence.md` | 700/1000 |

Verify with:
```bash
python -m devolaflow.agent_workspace.lint <change-id>   # agent-workspace artifacts
python -c "from devolaflow.agent_workspace import lint_human; print(lint_human())"  # .local/human/ surface
```
Soft over → warn; hard over → fail commit. Source: v15-ADR-008 §C-9;
human details: `references/human-surface.md` §4c.

# Workflow Rules (P3) — Development Process

## W-1 — Iteration Planning Gate (SI-1)

Before any version iteration, L0 MUST write a gap analysis in
`.local/research/` before implementation. It MUST list deficiencies, priorities,
and file-scoped fixes; this is the SI-2–SI-10 entry gate.

## W-2 — Harness-Driven Analysis (SI-2)

Iteration analysis MUST use repository evidence and the built-in evaluator:
```
python -m devolaflow.harness evaluate --ledger .local/telemetry/harness.jsonl --repo . --output .local/research/<cycle>_harness_evaluation.json
```
Run it again for end-of-iteration self-evaluation and store raw JSON in
`.local/research/`. Missing/insufficient evidence MUST remain `INSUFFICIENT`
until resolved or escalated. There is no external-tool or manual fallback
that bypasses the built-in evaluator.

## W-3 — Evaluation Before Release (SI-3)

Every pre-release needs a report covering Code quality (0.20), Architecture
(0.20), Tests (0.20), Maintainability (0.15), Compatibility (0.10), and
Performance (0.15); readiness is weighted composite ≥8.5/10.
External claims MUST NOT rely on a single seeded run; use more than one seeded
run and explicit reproducibility metadata: run identifier, caller-supplied salt
when present, source repository, and suitable variance or uncertainty evidence;
metadata or uncertainty evidence is `INSUFFICIENT`, never `PASS`; generated IDs
MUST NOT be called experimental salts.

## W-4 — Harness Regression Guard (SI-4)

Changes to selector/config/schema/SKILL/gate/harness modules MUST run and pass
`make test-harness`; context optimization compares token-injection
distributions, `quantifiable_ratio`, checklist completion, and
reversion/blocker trends with the W-16 baseline. Breaches are release blockers.
The comparison uses the active W-16 harness baseline.
Changes to `src/devolaflow/gate/` also MUST run
`python -m pytest tests/test_gate.py -v`.

## W-5 — Skill Format Coupling (SI-5)

Changes to SKILL.md or CLAUDE.md MUST check its line budget, run `build-skill`
for every HSC-registered adapter, pass `make test-harness`, and pass version
consistency; partial compliance is a violation. Changes to workflow-skill.yaml
also MUST verify core/data-driven adapters from `hosts.yaml` and
`adapter_configs/*.yaml` build within budget.

## W-6 — Context Budget Enforcement (SI-6)

Changes to `context_profiles.yaml` MUST run
`python -m devolaflow.task_adaptive_selector <task_type> --verbose` for every
affected type and verify relevant `critical` sections are retained while
unrelated sections are `skip`.

## W-7 — Iteration Retrospective (SI-8)

After each version release, store a `.local/research/` retrospective covering
gaps, implementation, deferrals/reasons, and learnings.

After W-16 settles cycle evidence, L0 MUST run:

```text
python scripts/archive_research_artifacts.py <cycle-version>
```

and commit the result under `docs/cycle-archive/<cycle-version>/`. Archiving is
idempotent: repeats preserve canonical contents without duplicates or clobbering.

Each cycle archive contains `README.md`, `gap_analysis.md`,
`implementation_plan.md`, `design/`, `harness/`, `evaluation/`, and
`retrospective.md` under `docs/cycle-archive/v<MAJOR>.<MINOR>.0/`.

W-16 settlement MUST precede archive creation. Patch releases create neither
independent baselines nor cycle archives. Historical contents are retained.

## W-8 — Convergence Round Reinforcement (SI-9)

Multi-round convergence MUST use `src/devolaflow/gate/reinforcement.py`, with
at most 5 severity-filtered rules per round. Stagnation for 2+ rounds MUST
escalate to human.

## W-9 — Test-Then-Commit Protocol (SI-10)

Every iteration MUST pass the six SI-10 gates in order:
1. `make test-core` — all tests pass
2. `ruff check src/ tests/`
3. `ruff format --check src/ tests/`
4. `make test-version`
5. `make test-harness`
6. `make check-cursor-skill`

`make precommit-full` aliases `release-preflight`; the Makefile is authoritative
for its six core gates and release-only extras. Single-execution is required:
no test runs twice in one chain, while `make test` remains the full suite.

## W-16 — Harness Baseline Settlement

Each MAJOR or MINOR cycle MUST settle its harness evidence exactly once in
`.local/telemetry/baselines/harness_baseline_<cycle>.json` at close or before
the next PV. Patch releases create no baseline. Every PV compares with that
settled artifact; retain current + previous two Tier-B files and archive older
ones in `docs/cycle-archive/<cycle>/harness/` (A-2.4 Tier C/W-7). Schema bumps
still require a new immutable `layout_invariant_v*.yaml` witness and all
Tier-A witnesses; settlement never regenerates, relocates, or prunes them.

## W-17 — Per-PV Test Cap Discipline (≤+30 NEW test functions per PV; mid-cycle audit at PV-05)

Each PV may add at most **+30 NEW test functions** (parameter expansions do not
count); cycle delta MUST stay ≤**+150**. At midpoint L0 MUST report cumulative
delta and forecast the remainder; if projected over +150, defer non-essential
tests. Count additions with `git diff <previous-tag>..HEAD -- tests/` and
`^\+\s*def test_`.

## W-18 — Ghost-Audit Refresh Precondition

Before CHANGELOG mentions a feature, `tests/ghost/` MUST cover it (S-4
precondition). Add its primary symbol to the current-cycle module, run
`python -m pytest tests/ghost/ -v`, then author the entry;
`tests/ghost/test_rules.py::test_ghost_audit_refresh_present` enforces this.

## W-20 — Env-Flag Reuse vs New-Flag Policy

Before authoring a NEW `DEVOLAFLOW_*` variable, L2 MUST consult
`references/env-flags.md` (canonical inventory) and apply **reuse-first**:

1. Same runtime surface? → REUSE it.
2. R5 pattern applies (read EXACTLY `"1"` + companion probe)? → MUST use
   that parsing and zero-IO off path.
3. Behaviorally orthogonal to every existing flag? → ONLY THEN author new.

A failed orthogonality test is a **W-20 violation**; reviewers MUST reject
(REUSE) or require the argument in the PR body linked to §7.

For a justified flag:

* add it to `references/env-flags.md` §2 in the same PR as its handler;
* add `tests/test_<feature>_disabled_is_noop.py` zero-IO coverage;
* cite it in CHANGELOG `## [vX.Y.Z]` under operator-visible behavior.

## W-21 — Soul-Set Freeze Governance

The Soul layer is frozen at its latest MAJOR/MINOR count. A proposed S-(N+1)
MUST, before landing, be telegraphed in cycle N's retrospective, re-entered
as SI-1 in N+2 with gap/enforcement evidence, and earn SI-3 architecture
≥9.5/10 in N+2. Keep Soul ≤12; later invariants belong in Architecture.
Current freeze: S-1..S-10. W-21 is human-gated; the 60-rule cap is enforced by
`tests/ghost/test_rules.py::test_rule_count_under_cap`.

## W-22 — Grill Mode Activation Contract

Grill mode is a natural-language, one-question interview; its contract and
implementation are `references/grill-mode.md` and
`src/devolaflow/skills/grill_mode.py`. `classify_grill_intent` returns
`GRILL_REQUESTED`, `GRILL_SUGGESTED`, or `NO_GRILL` for explicit, soft, or no
triggers.

### W-22.1 — Parallel-orthogonal composition with plan mode

PLAN and GRILL may coexist; when both are active, L0 MUST grill AC/scope FIRST,
then plan per `references/plan-mode-enforcement.md` §3. W-8/SI-9 and gen-verify
operate on artifacts, not utterances.

### W-22.2 — R5 strict default-OFF for auto-writes

Auto-writes to `CONTEXT.md`, `CONTEXT-MAP.md`, or `docs/adr/` MUST require
session consent; L0 MUST ask before writing. Companion: W-23.

### W-22.3 — 3-condition ADR gate (normative obligation)

For an ADR candidate, L0 MUST call
`devolaflow.skills.grill_mode.qualifies_as_adr(decision)` →
`(qualifies, missing_conditions)`. If false, L0 SHALL skip the offer and
surface failed conditions: Hard to reverse, Surprising without context, and
Real trade-off; all three are required.

### W-22.4 — W-20 env-flag reuse-first preservation

NO new `DEVOLAFLOW_*` flag is introduced: activation is solely
`classify_grill_intent`; see `references/env-flags.md` §2.

## W-23 — Domain Glossary Maintenance

When grill mode resolves a term, L0 MAY update the glossary per
`references/domain-awareness.md` (format/mechanics).

### W-23.1 — Lazy file creation

Create `CONTEXT.md` only for the first term, `CONTEXT-MAP.md` only for 2+
contexts, and `docs/adr/` only after W-22.3 passes. Repo-init MUST NOT create
them; operator consent remains required.

### W-23.2 — Opinionated-term discipline

The glossary MUST select ONE canonical term and list alternatives as `_Avoid_:`
aliases. `detect_fuzzy_terms(plan_text, glossary)` surfaces aliases;
`propose_canonical_term(candidate, glossary)` suggests the canonical term.

### W-23.3 — Project-specific scope

`CONTEXT.md` MUST contain only THIS project's domain terms; general programming
concepts DO NOT belong.

### W-23.4 — CONTEXT.md vs spec.md separation (per A-4)

`CONTEXT.md` is VOCABULARY; `.local/memory/specs/<domain>/spec.md` is BEHAVIOR.
They DO NOT overlap: terms go to `CONTEXT.md`, behavior decisions to
`.local/.agent/active/<id>/spec.md`.

### W-23.5 — Single vs multi-context layout inference

`infer_context_layout(repo_root)` returns `MULTI_CONTEXT` when
`CONTEXT-MAP.md` exists (map wins), `SINGLE_CONTEXT` for `CONTEXT.md`, else
`NO_CONTEXT_YET`; it is the only filesystem probe and MUST raise
`FileNotFoundError` for a missing root (S-5).

## W-24 — Subagent Pattern Selection

At wave decomposition, consult `references/subagent-patterns.md` and
`src/devolaflow/skills/subagent_pattern.py`. Supported patterns: **INLINE**
(one L2 via `Task`) and **FAN_OUT** (one L1, ≤5 parallel L2 tasks). **Teams
are permanently unsupported**: Soul P5 forbids shared state; reversal requires
SI-1, ADR, W-21 cadence, and SI-3 §3.2 ≥9.5/10.

### W-24.1 — Selection contract

`select_pattern(complexity, model_tier, task_count, parallel_independence)`
returns `"INLINE" | "FAN_OUT"` and NEVER `"TEAMS_FORBIDDEN"`; that literal is
reserved for `forbidden_pattern_rationale("TEAMS_FORBIDDEN")`.
### W-24.3 — Pattern 4 permanent-NOT-SUPPORTED rationale

The helper NEVER auto-returns `TEAMS_FORBIDDEN`; callers invoke the rationale
function explicitly for the P5 citation.

Source: v15-ADR-008 §W-24; taxonomy in `references/subagent-patterns.md`.

## W-25 — Host Support Contract Evidence and Revision

`workflow-system/agent/hosts.yaml` owns host identity, tiers, delivery floor,
and extras. A `boundary_bridge` MUST list `captured` or `vendor-doc`
provenance; the latter requires a `provenance_ref` URL, and
`synthetic`/`TBD-audit` cannot substantiate implementation. Adding a host,
channel, or axis MUST update schema, loader/parity tests, and current-cycle
ghost audit before claims. Unsupported capabilities remain `undeclared`,
`designed`, or `broken`; derived manifest views need parity checks. New axes
need design and evidence-backed tests; W-20 governs flags.

Source: v17.4.0 HSC design.

## W-26 — Local-Archive Deletion Safety (C-G4.3)

Deletion is permanently operator-only: no automatic deletion API/workflow for
`tasks`, `feedbacks`, or `research`; planning/clean checks never authorize it.
Runtime MUST NOT invoke `git clean -fdx` or equivalent. Dirty, ambiguous,
missing, unreadable, nested-repository, symlink, protected, or conflicted paths
MUST yield explicit refusal findings and remain in place. `.local/human/` and
`.local/.agent/` are never adapter inputs. See
`references/local-archive.md` §§6–7, `src/devolaflow/local/archive.py`,
`tests/test_local_archive.py`, `tests/test_local_archive_surfaces.py`, and the
current ghost audit.

## W-27 — Local-Archive Mapping Append-Only Behavior (C-G4.4)

Every physical move MUST append a record to its surface ledger:
`.local/tasks/archive-mappings.yaml`, `.local/feedbacks/archive/archive-mappings.yaml`,
or `.local/research/archive/archive-mappings.yaml`. Rows contain increasing
`sequence`, `source`, `destination`, `reason`, `timestamp`; existing rows are
immutable and duplicate source/destination MUST be refused. These are not
`.local/.agent/` handoffs; S-9 remains separate. See
`references/local-archive.md` §8, `src/devolaflow/local/archive.py::append_mapping_record`,
and cited local-archive tests/ghost audit.

## W-28 — Local-Archive Index-Generation Honesty (C-G4.5)

Each surface owns a generated index beside its ledger:
`.local/tasks/INDEX.md`, `.local/feedbacks/archive/INDEX.md`, or
`.local/research/archive/INDEX.md`. Output MUST carry its surface marker
(tasks: `<!-- devolaflow: generated task archive index -->`); only approved
apply may create a missing index. Human-maintained, symlinked, unreadable,
stale, or non-generated indexes MUST produce refusal/drift, never overwrite.
See `references/local-archive.md` §8, `src/devolaflow/local/archive.py::render_index`,
and cited tests/ghost audit.

## W-29 — Retro-Digest Evidence and Consent

Retro-Digest is natural-language only and MUST NOT add a `DEVOLAFLOW_*` flag or
CLI. Extraction MUST preserve verbatim source and repository-relative
provenance; L0 MAY select/label but MUST NOT rewrite it. Default is report-only;
writing `operational.jsonl` requires consent. Benefits stay report-only.
Missing evidence is `INSUFFICIENT`, never `PASS`. See
`references/retro-digest.md`.

## W-30 — Continuous Progress Contract

### W-30(a) — Bounded Wait and Ready-Work Progress

While a long-running external task is active (including CI, installation,
long tests, deployment, or an equivalent operation), agents MUST NOT idle or
meaninglessly poll. Every wait MUST have a timeout, heartbeat, and terminal
abandon/escalation path. When dependencies are satisfied and resources permit,
dispatchers MUST advance ready work instead of waiting.

### W-30(b) — Selective Blocker Isolation

After preflight, an ordinary blocker or `HUMAN_INTERVENE` finding pauses only
its affected item/task. Independent, unaffected siblings MUST continue. Reports MUST
distinguish `dependency-blocked` (waiting for a prerequisite),
`finding-blocked` (an unresolved finding), and `wave conflict` (ownership or
interface overlap). The workflow may stop only when no task can advance, or a
HARD breakpoint, preflight STOP card, `FULL_ROLLBACK`, ownership violation, or
destructive-policy violation requires it. A signed preflight does not waive
hard stops.

Primary references: `workflow-system/agent/references/execution-protocol.md`
§3, `references/decomposition-gate.md` §10, and
`references/wave-dispatch.md` §"Continuous progress and blocker isolation".

# Style Rules (P4) — Documentation & Presentation

## Documentation Sync (DS-*)

### ST-1 — Human-Facing Content Registry (DS-1)

On any iteration that affects users, reviewers, or the public site, review or explicitly confirm N/A for every path in the content registry:
- Primary docs: `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`
- Web demo primary IA: Home (`workflow-system/human/demo/index.html`), System (`framework-chain/`), I/O (`context-flow/`), Harness (`benchmark-results/`), Timeline (`version-timeline/`)
- Web demo compatibility routes: `design-system/`, `framework-chain/`, `context-flow/`, `version-timeline/`, `design-architecture/`, `workflow-visualizer/`, `stage-explorer/`, `benchmark-results/`, `blog/` (historical/editorial only; not current product truth)
- User guides EN: `workflow-system/human/en/` (8 files)
- User guides ZH: `workflow-system/human/zh/` (8 files)
- Design system: `workflow-system/human/demo/shared/` (styles.css, nav.js, i18n.js)
- CI/CD: `.github/workflows/*.yml`
- Build and demo-data pipeline: `scripts/build-site.sh`, `scripts/generate_human_docs.py`, `scripts/generate_demo_seed_catalog.py`

#### Demo Page Consistency Checklist

Before committing changes under `workflow-system/human/demo/`:
1. Every HTML page loads `shared/styles.css`
2. Every HTML page loads `shared/nav.js` and `shared/i18n.js`
3. No ad-hoc colors; use DS-2 palette
4. Every `data-i18n` key exists in both EN and ZH
5. Layout works at 640px width
6. Spot-check all pages at desktop and 640px width

### ST-2 — NieR: Automata Visual Identity (DS-2)

When editing web content under `workflow-system/human/demo/`:
- Colors: Gold accent `#B8860B`, Devola Red `#9B4444`, Warm Parchment `#F0EBE0`
- Typography: Cinzel (headers), Inter (body), JetBrains Mono (code)
- Tone: Warm, guardian-like (Devola), professional
- Consistency: Changes to colors/fonts/spacing on one page must be harmonized across all demo pages

### ST-3 — Bilingual Completeness (DS-3)

Any substantive update to a guide in `workflow-system/human/en/` requires a matching update in `workflow-system/human/zh/` (and vice versa). Adding or changing `data-i18n` keys requires both language dictionaries updated in the same commit.

#### Showcase Page Bilingual Completeness

Every `data-i18n` key in the four showcase pages MUST exist in both `en` and
`zh` blocks of `shared/i18n.js` or page-local `addTranslations` calls before
commit.

### ST-4 — Version Propagation in Human Docs (DS-4)

After bumping version, verify: demo `index.html` "What's New" and all EN/ZH files that mention the version. The `README.md` version badge and the `benchmark-results/index.html` displayed version are render/load-time DERIVED per C-6 (v14.4.0 G-031) — verify the derivation mechanism stays intact, not a literal. Run `make sync-human-docs` and `python -m pytest tests/test_version.py -v`.

#### Version Timeline Propagation

Whenever `__version__` changes, `workflow-system/human/demo/version-timeline/versions.json` MUST gain a new entry in the same PR. Required fields: version, date, era, headline, summary, highlights, metrics. Never invent metrics not stated in CHANGELOG.md.

## Web Experience (WX-*)

### ST-6 — Four Theme Showcases Are Mandatory (WX-1)

The four v6.3 theme pages (design-system, framework-chain, context-flow, version-timeline) are first-class deliverables. None may be removed without explicit retrospective entry, deprecation notice, nav update, and cross-page CTA update in the same PR.

#### Cross-Page CTA Cluster Integrity

The four theme pages MUST cross-link via footer/hero CTA clusters. Each page MUST carry a "Read SKILL" link to the GitHub URL. Minimum: 12 internal cross-links + 4 SKILL receipt links across the four pages.

### ST-8 — Motion Patterns Must Be Showcased (WX-3)

New `@keyframes` in `shared/styles.css` MUST appear as MotionShowcase in `design-system/index.html#ds-motion` in the same PR with: live demo, Replay button, duration/easing badge, i18n key in both EN/ZH, reduced-motion coverage.

#### Design Tokens Must Be Showcased

New CSS custom properties in `:root` MUST have dark-mode values AND a TokenSwatch in `design-system/index.html#ds-palette` in the same PR.

#### Components Must Be Showcased

New component class families in `shared/styles.css` MUST appear in `design-system/index.html#ds-components` with live example, component name in `<code>`, and i18n description.

### ST-11 — SKILL.md Section Changes Cascade to Showcase (WX-6)

When specific SKILL.md sections change, the corresponding showcase page sections MUST be updated verbatim in the same PR per CO-2.
